      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported an overall release on prior years' claims provisions of GBP 16.9m (approximately a 6.4% reduction against opening gross claims outstanding of GBP 264.4m). The improvement was broad-based by line, led by Property (fire and other damage to property GBP 4.9m), Marine (GBP 3.8m), Energy (GBP 2.7m), Reinsurance acceptances (GBP 2.8m) and Casualty (third party liability GBP 2.5m), and is attributed to favourable claims development on older years. The 2017 calendar year featured several named catastrophes (Harvey, Irma, Maria, Cyclone Debbie) which generated a modest combined net loss to the syndicate (report cites US$18m combined net loss), while other 2017 events such as the Mexico earthquake and California wildfires proved negligible for this syndicate.",
